## Original Content
ANALYSE - Un sondage d’une ampleur inédite auprès de 66 000 dirigeants est dévoilé à l’occasion de La REF 2026, la rentrée du Medef, qui se tient les 26 et 27 août à Roland-Garros. Si l’organisation patronale l’a placée sous le signe du « courage », les inquiétudes sont nombreuses.

## Summary
An unprecedented survey of 66,000 business leaders was revealed at La REF 2026, an event organized by Medef. The survey highlights widespread concerns among business leaders regarding taxation, charges, and bureaucracy, leading them to exert pressure on presidential candidates in the upcoming elections.

## Key Points
- A large-scale survey of 66,000 business leaders was conducted, marking an unprecedented scale.
- Key concerns identified include taxation, charges, and bureaucracy within the business environment.
- Business leaders are actively pressuring presidential candidates to address these issues.
- The survey was presented at Medef's event, La REF 2026, which focused on the theme of 'courage'.
- The findings reflect significant worries in the business community ahead of political elections.


